- `NPY_RAISE`: checks `j < 0 || j >= m`. If m == 0, then all j >= 0 satisfy `j >= 0`, so `j >= m` is true for any j >= 0. Wait, if j >= 0, then j >= 0 == m, so the condition `j >= m` is true, so it should raise. Hmm, but wait - if `j < 0`, then `j < 0` is true so it raises too. So for m == 0, RAISE should always raise for any j. Unless... the issue is `invalid = 1` is set and then `goto end_while`, which immediately ends. Then after the loop, if invalid, sets ValueError. So that path should work.

